The value of $r$ for which



\binom{20}{r}\binom{20}{0}+\binom{20}{r-1}\binom{20}{1}+\binom{20}{r-2}\binom{20}{2}+\ldots+\binom{20}{0}\binom{20}{r}

 is maximum, is:

questions.solution:
Consider the expression $\binom{20}{r}\binom{20}{0}+\binom{20}{r-1}\binom{20}{1}+\binom{20}{r-2}\binom{20}{2}+\ldots+\binom{20}{0} \cdot\binom{20}{r}$



For maximum value of above expression $r$ should be equal to 20 .

as



\begin{array}{l}

\binom{20}{20} \cdot\binom{20}{0}+\binom{20}{19} \cdot\binom{20}{1}+\ldots+\binom{20}{20} \cdot\binom{20}{0} \\

=\left(\binom{20}{0}\right)^{2}+\left(\binom{20}{1}\right)^{2}+\cdots+\left(\binom{20}{20}\right)^{2}=\binom{40}{20}

\end{array}



Which is the maximum value of the expression, So, $r=20$.

